  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Investment Fund for Pakistan (CIFPAK)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CIFPAK will mobilise private climate finance to support Pakistan&#x2019;s green growth and climate resilience ambitions.  Currently the 8th most climate vulnerable country in the world, the World Bank estimates that Pakistan will require US$348 billion of investment to become climate resilient and make the transition to a low-carbon economy by 2030. CIFPAK aims to crowd in private climate finance using a blended finance approach (public/private, concessional/non-concessional), supported by targeted technical assistance. It will have a specific focus on mobilising private investment for climate adaptation. The programme will support delivery of Pakistan&#x2019;s National Adaptation Plan and also aims to deepen Pakistan&#x2019;s capital markets. Programme&#x2019;s approved budget is &#xa3;108m (&#xa3;70m fiscal CDEL and &#xa3;38m RDEL) over seven years (April 2024 &#x2013; March 2031).</narrative>
  </description>
